<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jean-Baptiste Kléber</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1753–1800</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jean-Baptiste Kléber was a French general of the Revolutionary Wars from Strasbourg. He fought in the Vendée and on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a>, accompanied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon Bonaparte</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, and was left in command when Bonaparte returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> in 1799. After defeating an Ottoman army at Heliopolis in March 1800 and retaking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>, he was assassinated there in June 1800 by a Syrian student, Sulayman al-Halabi.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-baptiste-kleber.jpg" alt="Jean-Baptiste Kléber" width="320" height="375" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Urbain Guérin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_Jean_Baptiste_Kleber_(Jean_Gu%C3%A9rin)_-_Nationalmuseum_-_24145.tif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
